{"siren:A team is considering a four-day working week. Supporters argue that fewer interruptions could improve concentration and reduce staff turnover. However, the support desk must remain available five days a week. A small trial elsewhere reported higher satisfaction, but did not measure response times. One manager proposes a staggered schedule for three months, with service quality reviewed every fortnight.":"7fbcd0fce4963d7234d590a400aad2e68c5916f01e62343b0841e1165f42a2a7","lauren:Please confirm: you need twelve chairs, right?":"ef61a0e1548060db03b26f6b1bd5fd50800ad6eb36a43e4eeab34e4c67fdf1bc","lauren:The twenty-seventh is a Monday, and I teach on Tuesdays.":"16ec5b79b5c2d83acfcb5b884c28df9c728990cca18eb3f1d55786a29e7cf97c","lauren:That is all, thank you.":"e725c44691b36cb579ceacb2d5328c54d33bedef71625b1570aca620080e0919","lauren:Progress demands patience, progress demands persistence, progress demands purpose.":"340f52396be240aeec36ea55d2492af087acf55e17d655019e0aa0f0b8d66562","lauren:We gotta finish the report by Friday.":"a858138219db03223242ce8003a5eee1e3930dc0727fbf4d6624f587ec198292","lauren:What are your main strengths?":"58e29c1c0990175a73c1be5757f5eb766a081b896c3409fa24db5a8b70eb3fd3"}